1
00:00:00,542 --> 00:00:02,636
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

2
00:00:02,826 --> 00:00:04,088
(Crows caw)

3
00:00:04,461 --> 00:00:06,202
<i>(Frankie) Thanksgiving--</i>
<i>that time of year</i>

4
00:00:06,319 --> 00:00:08,016
<i>when the whole country</i>
<i>scurries about</i>

5
00:00:08,162 --> 00:00:10,954
<i>hunting and gathering</i>
<i>for the holiday feast.</i>

6
00:00:12,138 --> 00:00:13,478
(Clatters)

7
00:00:14,916 --> 00:00:16,102
What are you doing?

8
00:00:16,403 --> 00:00:18,867
Frugal Hoosier started
charging 10 cents for bags,

9
00:00:19,015 --> 00:00:20,393
so I told them
to find another sucker,

10
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:21,866
and I beat 'em
at their own game.

11
00:00:21,983 --> 00:00:23,258
Oh. Listen to this.

12
00:00:23,393 --> 00:00:25,848
I saw this flier that says
you can sign up

13
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:28,176
to host two Marines
at your Thanksgiving dinner.

14
00:00:28,306 --> 00:00:29,556
How cool would that be?

15
00:00:29,704 --> 00:00:32,048
Well, it depends on whose house
they're going to.

16
00:00:32,255 --> 00:00:33,839
Come on. It's the Marines.

17
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:35,375
We don't do anything
for this country.

18
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:37,909
All we have is that "support
our troops" bumper sticker,

19
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:40,009
and Axl turned it
into "support our poops."

20
00:00:40,112 --> 00:00:42,141
Plus Nancy Donahue
doesn't have any.

21
00:00:42,249 --> 00:00:43,776
We'd be the only ones
on the block.

22
00:00:43,889 --> 00:00:44,812
You really want to invite

23
00:00:44,929 --> 00:00:46,488
outside observers
into this place?

24
00:00:46,694 --> 00:00:48,828
I actually think it would
be nice to have guests.

25
00:00:48,966 --> 00:00:51,649
- We've already got your parents coming.
- They're not guests.

26
00:00:51,764 --> 00:00:55,179
- Sure feel like guests when they kick
me out of my bed. - (Sighs) Mike....

27
00:00:55,312 --> 00:00:57,808
Don't say my name and think you
can make me do stuff.

28
00:00:57,932 --> 00:00:59,722
Well, I was hoping
you'd have a different reaction,

29
00:00:59,901 --> 00:01:01,826
'cause I already signed us up.

30
00:01:01,932 --> 00:01:03,552
(Scoffs)
What? Why'd you even ask?

31
00:01:03,663 --> 00:01:05,094
Because I had to act quick.

32
00:01:05,207 --> 00:01:07,317
I was afraid they were gonna
run out of Marines.

33
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,867
There aren't that many
of them, you know.

34
00:01:08,998 --> 00:01:10,547
It's right there
in the motto--

35
00:01:10,671 --> 00:01:12,126
"The few, the proud."

36
00:01:12,818 --> 00:01:15,505
I gotta say, I thought you'd be
more patriotic about this.

37
00:01:15,612 --> 00:01:17,882
I am being patriotic. These
people fight for our country.

38
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:19,283
Haven't they
been through enough?

39
00:01:19,452 --> 00:01:21,478
Oh, crap. I think I left
the frozen food on the porch.

40
00:01:21,587 --> 00:01:22,781
Brick!

41
00:01:23,827 --> 00:01:25,612
(Door closes)
This book is life-changing.

42
00:01:25,775 --> 00:01:27,318
Mom dropped me at the library

43
00:01:27,428 --> 00:01:28,796
to find
the perfect holiday read,

44
00:01:28,915 --> 00:01:30,790
and out of nowhere,
it just appeared to me.

45
00:01:34,453 --> 00:01:36,242
"The real true
behind-the-scenes story

46
00:01:36,364 --> 00:01:40,919
of the making of Erich Segal's
1970's classic, Love Story."

47
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:43,007
Really? All the books
they got in the library,

48
00:01:43,182 --> 00:01:44,260
and that's the one you picked?

49
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:46,457
Have you read it?
It's fascinating.

50
00:01:46,651 --> 00:01:48,857
How did I go so long
without finding this?

51
00:01:48,957 --> 00:01:50,561
It's a Thanksgiving gift,
I tell you.

52
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:51,868
A gift.

53
00:01:53,725 --> 00:01:55,281
You know, the only thing
that would have made that better

54
00:01:55,386 --> 00:01:57,330
is if strangers
were here to see it.

55
00:01:58,213 --> 00:01:59,575
<i>Meanwhile,</i>
<i>Brick wasn't the only one</i>

56
00:01:59,665 --> 00:02:01,743
<i>with a fascination</i>
<i>for the library.</i>

57
00:02:01,893 --> 00:02:02,904
<i>Over the past few weeks,</i>

58
00:02:03,003 --> 00:02:06,043
<i>Axl had become very focused</i>
<i>on his studies.</i>

59
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:08,578
So the biggest thing you need
to study for your test is...

60
00:02:09,155 --> 00:02:11,037
"The legislative branch."

61
00:02:12,093 --> 00:02:13,019
Wow.

62
00:02:13,116 --> 00:02:14,219
Your handwriting's pretty...

63
00:02:14,316 --> 00:02:15,865
Terrible.
Uh, but I can say that

64
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:17,542
'cause my handwriting
is awesome.

65
00:02:17,724 --> 00:02:19,471
Maybe I need
a handwriting tutor.

66
00:02:20,041 --> 00:02:22,340
Maybe you do. (Chuckles)

67
00:02:23,305 --> 00:02:23,826
(Scribbling)

68
00:02:23,949 --> 00:02:25,038
"Axl...

69
00:02:25,135 --> 00:02:26,187
is...

70
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:28,414
brilliant."

71
00:02:29,515 --> 00:02:30,697
Pretty impressive, huh?

72
00:02:30,799 --> 00:02:32,465
Uh-huh. It'd be
even more impressive

73
00:02:32,573 --> 00:02:34,815
if you spelled "brilliant"
with two L's.

74
00:02:35,324 --> 00:02:36,332
(Both laugh)

75
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,107
(Cell phone ringing)

76
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:41,185
Oh, it's my boyfriend
calling from Northwestern.

77
00:02:41,336 --> 00:02:42,619
I should take this.

78
00:02:42,816 --> 00:02:44,725
Cool. Cool. Cool.

79
00:02:44,826 --> 00:02:46,903
Yeah, I gotta get
to the foot doctor anyway.

80
00:02:47,336 --> 00:02:50,141
(Clears throat) You know.
I'll see you later,

81
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:52,696
and just don't worry
about, uh, anything.

82
00:02:53,989 --> 00:02:55,044
Just... uh, good luck.

83
00:02:55,191 --> 00:02:55,835
(School bell rings)

84
00:02:55,945 --> 00:02:58,404
Okay, no unauthorized
non-mascots are allowed in here,

85
00:02:58,548 --> 00:03:01,583
so tell nobody
what you are about to see.

86
00:03:02,936 --> 00:03:04,453
(Clank)

87
00:03:05,105 --> 00:03:06,046
(Doors creak)

88
00:03:06,842 --> 00:03:08,051
Where's the head?

89
00:03:08,175 --> 00:03:10,755
Brad, the head is gone!

90
00:03:11,717 --> 00:03:12,607
Gone!

91
00:03:12,804 --> 00:03:14,071
The crack in my foot is gone!

92
00:03:14,189 --> 00:03:15,378
The Ax Man's back in the game!

93
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:17,477
Stomp on my foot!
Go ahead! I'm healed!

94
00:03:17,589 --> 00:03:18,975
I'm a medical miracle!

95
00:03:19,090 --> 00:03:20,121
Are you serious?

96
00:03:20,228 --> 00:03:21,378
Doctor says as long
as he's not in pain,

97
00:03:21,485 --> 00:03:22,379
he's good to go.

98
00:03:22,502 --> 00:03:23,884
Does that mean
he can play Friday?

99
00:03:23,994 --> 00:03:25,060
With the recruiters there?

100
00:03:25,201 --> 00:03:26,374
Yep. We might not
have to pay for college

101
00:03:26,488 --> 00:03:27,726
with our kidneys after all.

102
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:30,445
(Squeals) Oh!
(Laughs)

103
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:31,261
Oh, Mike!

104
00:03:31,362 --> 00:03:32,656
You know what?
I'm telling you, Mike,

105
00:03:32,755 --> 00:03:34,200
us opening our hearts
to the Marines

106
00:03:34,317 --> 00:03:35,717
is the reason
he got better so fast.

107
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:37,343
You put good
out into the world,

108
00:03:37,455 --> 00:03:38,934
and good comes back to you.

109
00:03:39,147 --> 00:03:42,530
(Doorbell rings) (Grunts)

110
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:45,134
(Sighs) We would have been here
two hours ago!

111
00:03:45,244 --> 00:03:47,288
But Vasco de Gama here decided

112
00:03:47,425 --> 00:03:50,085
to take one
of his legendary shortcuts.

113
00:03:50,225 --> 00:03:53,657
He got so lost,
we never got to stop at Costco!

114
00:03:53,774 --> 00:03:56,498
What, so you couldn't get
your giant pop and hot dog?

115
00:03:56,628 --> 00:03:58,845
Do you know how many carbs
are in one of them buns?

116
00:03:58,948 --> 00:03:59,907
You lose 4 pounds,

117
00:04:00,014 --> 00:04:02,055
and suddenly
you're Jack Lalanne!

118
00:04:04,371 --> 00:04:06,646
- Happy Thanksgiving!
- Happy Thanksgiving!

119
00:04:07,388 --> 00:04:08,546
<i>And come hell or high water,</i>

120
00:04:08,659 --> 00:04:10,405
<i>I was determined</i>
<i>it was gonna be.</i>

121
00:04:10,769 --> 00:04:13,614
<i>'Cause turns out we had a lot</i>
<i>to be grateful for this year.</i>

122
00:04:13,906 --> 00:04:16,202
<i>And Axl couldn't wait</i>
<i>to share the good news.</i>

123
00:04:16,661 --> 00:04:19,334
I'm cured!
The Ax Man has riseth!

124
00:04:19,451 --> 00:04:20,909
Or is it "risen-eth"?
Doesn't matter.

125
00:04:21,046 --> 00:04:22,279
'Cause my foot
healed three weeks early.

126
00:04:22,437 --> 00:04:25,854
(Thud) Stomp on my foot. Go ahead.
Honestly. I'm fine. (Laughs)

127
00:04:25,955 --> 00:04:28,009
Wow, that's great, Axl,
but I'm kind of busy here.

128
00:04:28,146 --> 00:04:29,736
Gene has a big test
on world War II tomorrow.

129
00:04:29,852 --> 00:04:32,010
Well, grab a pencil, Gene.
We won.

130
00:04:32,123 --> 00:04:33,647
And you know who else
is gonna win Friday night?

131
00:04:33,835 --> 00:04:35,603
Orson, when we kick
Roosevelt's butt!

132
00:04:35,713 --> 00:04:36,961
So you're actually
gonna play in the game?

133
00:04:37,084 --> 00:04:38,459
You really think
that's a good idea?

134
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:41,525
Uh, it's not just <i>a game,</i>
it's the championship,

135
00:04:41,637 --> 00:04:42,455
which reminds me,

136
00:04:42,566 --> 00:04:44,147
I'm gonna have to start
leaving our sessions early

137
00:04:44,258 --> 00:04:45,432
for practice, but...

138
00:04:45,573 --> 00:04:46,802
Great. So you're gonna
skip studying

139
00:04:46,934 --> 00:04:48,865
so you can go bash your head
into other guys' heads.

140
00:04:49,001 --> 00:04:50,174
Sounds like a super solid plan.

141
00:04:50,281 --> 00:04:52,008
You know what? Why don't we
just skip it altogether?

142
00:04:52,185 --> 00:04:54,368
Wow. You know what you
<i>should</i> tutor people on?

143
00:04:54,492 --> 00:04:56,190
How to ruin
the world's greatest moment,

144
00:04:56,289 --> 00:04:57,685
'cause you are awesome at it.

145
00:04:57,803 --> 00:04:59,021
I don't know
what to tell you, Axl.

146
00:04:59,148 --> 00:04:59,907
Sorry this didn't happen

147
00:05:00,023 --> 00:05:01,345
the way you played it
all out in your head.

148
00:05:01,459 --> 00:05:02,237
Let me tell you something.

149
00:05:02,350 --> 00:05:05,458
This is not a normal response
to awesome news, okay?

150
00:05:06,266 --> 00:05:08,677
Guess what?! Playing in
the championship Friday!

151
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:10,219
(Cheers and applause)

152
00:05:10,522 --> 00:05:12,111
That was a normal response.

153
00:05:21,719 --> 00:05:23,487
I've checked everywhere,
and it's nowhere.

154
00:05:23,625 --> 00:05:25,189
Not the dry cleaners,
not the pizza place,

155
00:05:25,314 --> 00:05:27,886
not the bleachers where I watch
the guy mow the lawn.

156
00:05:28,019 --> 00:05:30,024
The school trusted me
with its mascot,

157
00:05:30,142 --> 00:05:32,500
and I have let everyone down.

158
00:05:32,673 --> 00:05:34,038
This is a disaster!

159
00:05:34,752 --> 00:05:36,985
I'm literally a chicken
with its head cut off.

160
00:05:37,104 --> 00:05:39,838
<i>Well, she wasn't the only one.</i>
<i>Three days until Thanksgiving,</i>

161
00:05:39,953 --> 00:05:42,167
<i>and we were</i>
<i>nowhere near Marine-ready.</i>

162
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:45,039
Ugh! I just want everything
to look right for the Marines.

163
00:05:45,161 --> 00:05:48,380
If I use this picture
to cover the wallpaper scar,

164
00:05:48,493 --> 00:05:49,544
does that look okay?

165
00:05:49,657 --> 00:05:51,479
I'd lower it, like, 2 inches.

166
00:05:51,605 --> 00:05:54,469
Yeah, listen to her.
She's the expert on everything.

167
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,079
I married Mrs. Right.

168
00:05:56,232 --> 00:05:58,327
I just didn't know
her first name was "always."

169
00:05:58,615 --> 00:05:59,778
(Sighs)
(Brick) Get this--

170
00:05:59,906 --> 00:06:01,466
apparently,
the scenes in Love Story

171
00:06:01,583 --> 00:06:04,364
with Oliver walking through
a snowy New York were added

172
00:06:04,491 --> 00:06:06,879
after principal photography
was completed.

173
00:06:07,125 --> 00:06:07,935
<i>After!</i>

174
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:10,253
Oh, I just adored Love Story.

175
00:06:10,401 --> 00:06:13,632
Hey, Brick, why don't
I rent us a copy,

176
00:06:13,752 --> 00:06:15,438
and you and I
can watch it together?

177
00:06:15,839 --> 00:06:17,186
Why would we do that?

178
00:06:17,371 --> 00:06:20,917
I'm with you, Brick.
Love Story was a lousy movie.

179
00:06:21,028 --> 00:06:21,888
What do <i>you</i> know?

180
00:06:22,009 --> 00:06:24,267
You slept through it
like every movie we see.

181
00:06:24,381 --> 00:06:26,550
Then you woke up
and said it didn't make sense.

182
00:06:26,657 --> 00:06:27,997
I'll tell you
what was a good picture.

183
00:06:28,113 --> 00:06:29,845
The Longest Day.
You ever see that?

184
00:06:30,019 --> 00:06:31,950
Don't need to.
I'm living it.

185
00:06:32,524 --> 00:06:33,669
(Vacuum whirring)

186
00:06:34,354 --> 00:06:35,662
(Exhales deeply)

187
00:06:37,091 --> 00:06:38,640
Ugh. Jeez.

188
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:40,706
What is wrong with my parents?

189
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:42,660
You're gonna
have to be more specific.

190
00:06:42,789 --> 00:06:45,276
The bickering.
It's nuts, right?

191
00:06:45,389 --> 00:06:47,298
I don't get it. I mean,
it seems to be getting worse.

192
00:06:47,408 --> 00:06:48,532
It's worse, right?

193
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,083
Frankie, they've
been together 50 years.

194
00:06:50,317 --> 00:06:51,391
Just be happy
they're not starring

195
00:06:51,524 --> 00:06:53,611
in a Dateline unsolved mystery.

196
00:06:53,845 --> 00:06:55,671
(Sighs)
Well, I'm almost wondering

197
00:06:55,797 --> 00:06:58,505
if having the Marines here
is a good idea at all.

198
00:06:58,624 --> 00:07:00,669
- Now you're wondering?
- You know what it is?

199
00:07:00,870 --> 00:07:02,187
They've been alone too long.

200
00:07:02,398 --> 00:07:05,234
Maybe we need to remind them
why they love each other.

201
00:07:05,353 --> 00:07:07,010
Like, reboot their brains

202
00:07:07,164 --> 00:07:08,934
so they start being nice
to each other again.

203
00:07:09,418 --> 00:07:11,569
(Tag) What'd you do
with my goji berries?

204
00:07:11,718 --> 00:07:14,460
(Pat) Oh, yeah, I live
<i>to hide your goji berries!</i>

205
00:07:14,617 --> 00:07:16,156
Good luck with that.

206
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,025
(School bell rings)

207
00:07:24,357 --> 00:07:25,202
(Gasps)

208
00:07:26,155 --> 00:07:27,501
(Dog barks in distance)

209
00:07:28,651 --> 00:07:29,948
Come on.
I'll throw you a couple.

210
00:07:30,058 --> 00:07:32,216
No, thanks.
I'm kind of busy here.

211
00:07:32,775 --> 00:07:34,234
You're poking the earth
with a stick.

212
00:07:35,043 --> 00:07:36,510
What's going on with you, Axl?

213
00:07:36,626 --> 00:07:38,687
You got a huge game Friday.
The big comeback.

214
00:07:38,813 --> 00:07:40,187
Everybody from school's
gonna be there.

215
00:07:40,551 --> 00:07:41,662
Not everybody.

216
00:07:42,022 --> 00:07:42,881
What's that mean?

217
00:07:43,283 --> 00:07:44,244
Nothing.

218
00:07:45,179 --> 00:07:45,860
Hmm.

219
00:07:47,581 --> 00:07:49,439
So... (Clears throat)
Help me out here.

220
00:07:50,008 --> 00:07:51,178
The other day
when the doctor said

221
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,663
you could play
in the game on Friday,

222
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,143
weren't you the guy
who asked him

223
00:07:54,236 --> 00:07:55,128
if you could kiss him
on the mouth?

224
00:07:55,231 --> 00:07:57,926
Yeah. I was excited,
but then I started thinkin'...

225
00:07:58,128 --> 00:08:00,726
(Sighs) You know,
this whole studying thing

226
00:08:00,822 --> 00:08:01,779
is kind of working out for me.

227
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,179
Maybe I should just
stick to that.

228
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:04,271
Studying.

229
00:08:04,628 --> 00:08:07,541
Okay. I think I know
what's going on here.

230
00:08:07,852 --> 00:08:10,436
You're nervous.
You haven't played in a while.

231
00:08:10,537 --> 00:08:12,465
There's a lot riding
on this game. I get that, Axl.

232
00:08:12,565 --> 00:08:14,563
But sometimes you just gotta
lay it all out there

233
00:08:14,704 --> 00:08:15,989
and go for it.

234
00:08:16,722 --> 00:08:18,112
I don't know.

235
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:20,814
Trust me. Don't ever
let fear stop you

236
00:08:20,930 --> 00:08:22,533
from going after what you want.

237
00:08:25,711 --> 00:08:28,226
<i>Mike's advice</i>
<i>really hit home for Axl...</i>

238
00:08:29,151 --> 00:08:31,493
<i>Just not exactly</i>
<i>the way Mike had intended.</i>

239
00:08:31,596 --> 00:08:33,173
Cassidy, I like you.

240
00:08:33,834 --> 00:08:35,353
(Door closes) I never really saw
myself with a girl like you before.

241
00:08:35,468 --> 00:08:36,727
You know, I usually
just go for hot chicks.

242
00:08:36,984 --> 00:08:38,214
Not that you're...
(Chuckles) not hot.

243
00:08:38,329 --> 00:08:39,884
It's just you're just hot
in a different way.

244
00:08:40,036 --> 00:08:41,751
Um, you use words
like "perseverating"

245
00:08:41,884 --> 00:08:43,991
and "truncated," which is
a really cool word for "short,"

246
00:08:44,096 --> 00:08:45,830
but I never knew that
until I met you.

247
00:08:45,930 --> 00:08:47,852
And I have so many things
to say to you,

248
00:08:47,952 --> 00:08:49,680
but I'll try
to keep it truncated. (Chuckles)

249
00:08:49,785 --> 00:08:50,779
I like hanging out with you.

250
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:52,818
I think it's cool
that you think I can be smart

251
00:08:52,925 --> 00:08:54,107
and you listen to violin music,

252
00:08:54,221 --> 00:08:55,693
and you watch movies
with the typing at the bottom.

253
00:08:55,797 --> 00:08:57,836
And my whole life,
I have loved football,

254
00:08:57,932 --> 00:08:59,930
but it's weird, 'cause it just
doesn't seem to matter to me

255
00:09:00,038 --> 00:09:00,987
if it doesn't matter to you.

256
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,013
And I want you to come
to my game, Cassidy.

257
00:09:03,225 --> 00:09:05,313
And I know you have this guy
who calls you from college,

258
00:09:05,432 --> 00:09:06,708
but he's not here now,
and I am,

259
00:09:06,810 --> 00:09:08,736
and I like you, and I think
you should go out with me.

260
00:09:09,948 --> 00:09:10,739
(Chuckles nervously)

261
00:09:10,864 --> 00:09:14,451
Oh. Wow, Axl. That's...

262
00:09:14,596 --> 00:09:15,455
a lot.

263
00:09:15,602 --> 00:09:17,836
Seriously, that is all
so nice of you to say,

264
00:09:17,963 --> 00:09:19,373
but I-I just--

265
00:09:19,671 --> 00:09:21,944
see, my boyfriend's coming
to spend Thanksgiving with me,

266
00:09:22,077 --> 00:09:24,528
so I don't think
I can come to your game,

267
00:09:24,716 --> 00:09:25,778
but thanks.

268
00:09:25,922 --> 00:09:28,122
I mean, yeah, thank you.

269
00:09:30,139 --> 00:09:32,403
Uh... (Chuckles nervously)
Yeah, cool. Cool. Cool.

270
00:09:32,519 --> 00:09:33,618
Uh... (Clears throat)
You know... (Laughs)

271
00:09:33,772 --> 00:09:35,991
I just... I'm asking
everybody to my game,

272
00:09:36,154 --> 00:09:38,942
not just you. So...
(Inhales deeply)

273
00:09:39,047 --> 00:09:41,889
Hey! Anybody wanna go watch me
play football Friday night?

274
00:09:41,991 --> 00:09:44,223
I'd love to, Axl.
Can I bring my snake?

275
00:09:53,989 --> 00:09:55,081
What do you think?

276
00:09:55,246 --> 00:09:57,181
Well, that depends.
Is there gonna be a president

277
00:09:57,296 --> 00:09:58,959
giving a speech
off the back of a train?

278
00:09:59,112 --> 00:10:01,856
(Refrigerator door opens) I just want
it to look patriotic for the Marines,

279
00:10:01,981 --> 00:10:03,233
to show we care, you know?

280
00:10:03,350 --> 00:10:05,690
Because they do
so much for our country.

281
00:10:05,818 --> 00:10:07,495
It's the least we can do
for them.

282
00:10:07,637 --> 00:10:09,826
Wow. Okay, can I tell you guys
one more thing?

283
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,091
- No.
- Nobody cares, Brick.

284
00:10:11,199 --> 00:10:12,640
Who do you think
was the studio's first choice

285
00:10:12,771 --> 00:10:14,000
for the part of Oliver?

286
00:10:14,853 --> 00:10:18,314
It was Beau Bridges.
Can you believe it? Uh...

287
00:10:19,583 --> 00:10:20,645
Who's Beau Bridges?

288
00:10:20,752 --> 00:10:23,367
I asked you to do one thing--
pack my ginkgo biloba.

289
00:10:23,479 --> 00:10:24,854
They're <i>your</i> ginkgo biloba.

290
00:10:24,969 --> 00:10:26,207
You want 'em,
you gonna pack 'em.

291
00:10:26,315 --> 00:10:28,816
- You're a grown man, for God sake.
- They're for my memory!

292
00:10:28,992 --> 00:10:30,443
How in the hell am I
supposed to remember 'em

293
00:10:30,567 --> 00:10:31,419
if I don't take 'em?

294
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:33,610
Mom, dad, Mike and I
were trying to remember

295
00:10:33,729 --> 00:10:37,187
that great story you always tell
about your first date.

296
00:10:37,318 --> 00:10:39,542
You know, how dad got lost
and you ended up by the lake?

297
00:10:39,651 --> 00:10:40,449
What happened again?

298
00:10:40,568 --> 00:10:42,104
(Chuckles)
Oh, he got lost all right.

299
00:10:42,248 --> 00:10:43,724
No surprise there.

300
00:10:43,848 --> 00:10:47,524
- Yeah, she was probably talking so much,
I missed the sign. - No, it was sweet.

301
00:10:47,644 --> 00:10:49,479
You got lost and you
didn't have anything to eat,

302
00:10:49,603 --> 00:10:51,620
and mom pulled the crackers
from her bag and--

303
00:10:51,732 --> 00:10:53,013
Back then,
he would <i>eat</i> crackers!

304
00:10:53,129 --> 00:10:54,557
Crackers are poison!

305
00:10:54,794 --> 00:10:56,366
Might as well
eat a bag of sugar!

306
00:10:59,018 --> 00:11:00,145
Oh. Excuse me.

307
00:11:00,273 --> 00:11:01,403
Can we have
a word with you gentlemen?

308
00:11:01,606 --> 00:11:02,291
Sure.

309
00:11:02,474 --> 00:11:03,479
We would have
talked to you earlier,

310
00:11:03,585 --> 00:11:04,947
but we didn't want
to disrupt your rehearsal.

311
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:05,920
Practice.

312
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:08,791
Which one of you
is captain of this company?

313
00:11:09,122 --> 00:11:10,532
Team. He meant "team."

314
00:11:10,662 --> 00:11:12,654
Look, we know
you stole our mascot head.

315
00:11:12,806 --> 00:11:14,757
So the joke is over.
We want it back.

316
00:11:14,955 --> 00:11:17,502
Oh, no. You lost your head?
I guess it's true what they say

317
00:11:17,621 --> 00:11:19,967
about how the body still runs
around without its head.

318
00:11:20,126 --> 00:11:22,628
See you Friday night, losers.

319
00:11:22,915 --> 00:11:26,480
- That's it. There's only one
way to settle this. - No! Brad!

320
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:28,787
Dance fight! Five, six, seven, eight...
(Snaps fingers)

321
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:31,411
Who punches a guy
while he's on his tippy toes?

322
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:33,291
That's not
how a dance fight works.

323
00:11:33,476 --> 00:11:36,629
I mean, seriously, where did
that guy go to summer camp?

324
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:38,131
Ugh. I know.

325
00:11:39,121 --> 00:11:40,912
I didn't even get to do
my pas de bourree.

326
00:11:41,019 --> 00:11:41,846
Aw.

327
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:45,604
<i>(Tv playing indistinctly)</i> In Mexico,
it's known as <i>Historia de Amor.</i>

328
00:11:45,814 --> 00:11:48,862
In Finland, it's <i>Rakkaustarina.</i>

329
00:11:49,091 --> 00:11:50,472
I feel like
you're not listening.

330
00:11:50,817 --> 00:11:51,673
That's because I'm not, Brick.

331
00:11:51,785 --> 00:11:53,066
The Marines are gonna
be here any minute.

332
00:11:53,248 --> 00:11:56,584
Axl, put on some clothes
and comb your hair!

333
00:11:56,751 --> 00:11:59,352
To what end, mom?
To what end?

334
00:11:59,532 --> 00:12:00,554
(Sighs)

335
00:12:00,868 --> 00:12:02,040
Mike, I'm gonna be busy
with the Marines,

336
00:12:02,172 --> 00:12:02,913
so you're in charge

337
00:12:03,026 --> 00:12:04,329
of corralling the bickermans
at dinner.

338
00:12:04,508 --> 00:12:06,515
How come you get the Marines,
and I get your parents?

339
00:12:06,622 --> 00:12:07,796
Because you didn't want
the Marines here.

340
00:12:07,954 --> 00:12:09,722
In my defense, I didn't want
your parents here, either.

341
00:12:09,888 --> 00:12:11,214
(Doorbell rings) Oh!

342
00:12:11,371 --> 00:12:12,206
Okay, that's them.

343
00:12:12,326 --> 00:12:14,155
Quick,
everybody put your flag pins on.

344
00:12:17,257 --> 00:12:19,217
Well, hello there.

345
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:21,084
(Laughs) Wow, we got
a couple of good ones.

346
00:12:21,207 --> 00:12:22,581
Hi. I'm Frankie Heck.

347
00:12:22,738 --> 00:12:24,044
Corporal Nick Martinez.

348
00:12:24,227 --> 00:12:25,529
Sergeant Justin Howard.

349
00:12:25,787 --> 00:12:26,594
We can't thank you enough

350
00:12:26,713 --> 00:12:27,954
for inviting us
into your home, ma'am.

351
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:30,262
Oh, please.
It's the least we could do.

352
00:12:30,365 --> 00:12:32,484
You do so much for us.
(Chuckles)

353
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:36,458
Wow. I love your uniforms--
the badges and the stripes.

354
00:12:36,575 --> 00:12:39,950
I don't know what they mean,
but you must be very brave.

355
00:12:40,313 --> 00:12:41,518
Hey, Nancy!

356
00:12:41,649 --> 00:12:43,796
Just having dinner
with America's heroes--

357
00:12:43,932 --> 00:12:44,790
two of 'em!

358
00:12:44,896 --> 00:12:46,204
Happy Thanksgiving!

359
00:12:46,306 --> 00:12:47,656
So the screenplay
was turned down

360
00:12:47,788 --> 00:12:49,326
by every studio in Hollywood,

361
00:12:49,442 --> 00:12:52,823
but Segal's agent, Howard Minsky
of the William Morris Agency--

362
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,374
This is my son Brick.

363
00:12:54,481 --> 00:12:55,471
(Book thuds)
That's my other son Axl.

364
00:12:55,579 --> 00:12:57,110
He's just waiting
for the iron to heat up

365
00:12:57,232 --> 00:12:58,935
so he can press his slacks.

366
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:00,322
What are slacks?

367
00:13:00,429 --> 00:13:01,730
(Teeth clenched) Get dressed.

368
00:13:01,856 --> 00:13:03,683
Mom, does this say
"chicken" to you?

369
00:13:03,876 --> 00:13:05,804
This is my daughter Sue.

370
00:13:06,106 --> 00:13:08,510
And oh, this is
my great aunt Edie,

371
00:13:08,643 --> 00:13:11,515
and my parents Pat and Tag,
and my husband Mike.

372
00:13:11,684 --> 00:13:13,335
You have
a very beautiful home, sir.

373
00:13:13,538 --> 00:13:16,219
Well, you've seen too many
bombed-out cities, but thanks.

374
00:13:16,332 --> 00:13:19,101
So, um, Corporal,
why don't you sit there,

375
00:13:19,287 --> 00:13:21,287
and, Sergeant,
you can sit there.

376
00:13:21,387 --> 00:13:23,170
So it'll be
Marine-Frankie-Marine.

377
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,333
Just like a Marine sandwich.
(Laughs)

378
00:13:26,394 --> 00:13:27,900
Or we can sit wherever.

379
00:13:28,018 --> 00:13:31,268
Look at this. All poison.
I can't eat any of it.

380
00:13:31,386 --> 00:13:33,134
Eat it, don't eat it.
Nobody cares.

381
00:13:33,245 --> 00:13:34,302
Hey, you two lovebirds
don't mind

382
00:13:34,413 --> 00:13:35,752
if I squeeze in here, do ya?

383
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,506
Well, shall we get started?

384
00:13:39,609 --> 00:13:44,124
I pledge allegiance to the flag
of the United States of America.

385
00:13:45,454 --> 00:13:46,743
Just wanted
to get that out there.

386
00:13:46,859 --> 00:13:48,889
You know,
where my allegiance lies.

387
00:13:49,744 --> 00:13:51,386
So before we eat, um,

388
00:13:51,527 --> 00:13:52,855
why don't we go
around the table

389
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,423
and everybody say
what they're thankful for?

390
00:13:54,525 --> 00:13:56,305
It's kind of
our Thanksgiving tradition.

391
00:13:56,443 --> 00:13:57,800
- It is?
- Since when?

392
00:13:57,945 --> 00:13:59,371
(Clears throat) I'll start.

393
00:13:59,909 --> 00:14:03,269
Well, I'm thankful
for the freedom

394
00:14:03,408 --> 00:14:06,605
that you two provide
with your guns and stuff.

395
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,549
And I have to say, I, for one,

396
00:14:08,716 --> 00:14:11,453
have never felt
so safe in my own home.

397
00:14:12,492 --> 00:14:14,028
I'm thankful
for all my fellow Marines

398
00:14:14,149 --> 00:14:16,282
who put themselves
in harm's way every day

399
00:14:16,469 --> 00:14:18,303
so we can all live and prosper

400
00:14:18,423 --> 00:14:20,173
in the greatest country
in the world.

401
00:14:21,221 --> 00:14:23,262
I'm thankful that
the theme from Love Story

402
00:14:23,429 --> 00:14:26,061
hit number 39
on the US music charts.

403
00:14:26,194 --> 00:14:29,370
I'm thankful I'm still running
on my own steam.

404
00:14:29,538 --> 00:14:30,323
(Giggles)

405
00:14:30,436 --> 00:14:31,981
What the hell's that mean?
Don't make any sense.

406
00:14:32,176 --> 00:14:35,182
I think I'm allowed
to say what I'm thankful for

407
00:14:35,311 --> 00:14:37,621
without comments
from the peanut gallery.

408
00:14:37,779 --> 00:14:39,463
I'd like to go in a different
direction this year

409
00:14:39,594 --> 00:14:41,507
and say what I am not
thankful for.

410
00:14:41,690 --> 00:14:43,993
I am not thankful
for Roosevelt High,

411
00:14:44,134 --> 00:14:46,539
specifically the football
players at Roosevelt High,

412
00:14:46,693 --> 00:14:48,054
who cheat at dance fights

413
00:14:48,192 --> 00:14:49,796
and steal
people's chicken heads.

414
00:14:50,616 --> 00:14:52,256
- Axl?
- Pass.

415
00:14:52,844 --> 00:14:55,295
- Aunt Edie?
- Merry Christmas!

416
00:14:55,462 --> 00:14:57,503
I'm thankful that's over.
Who wants some potatoes?

417
00:14:57,627 --> 00:14:59,437
Wait a minute, wait a minute.
I-I didn't get my turn.

418
00:14:59,566 --> 00:15:00,402
I was gonna tell the story

419
00:15:00,527 --> 00:15:02,546
about how when I was
stationed in Korea--

420
00:15:02,678 --> 00:15:03,930
You were a file clerk.

421
00:15:04,050 --> 00:15:06,010
(Tag) Hey, there was a lot
of tension in that office!

422
00:15:06,202 --> 00:15:07,796
Um, hey, uh,

423
00:15:07,975 --> 00:15:12,136
so, uh, I bet being
a Marine... keeps you busy.

424
00:15:12,308 --> 00:15:14,451
Actually, we just did
a recon mission if Afghanistan

425
00:15:14,590 --> 00:15:16,128
to recover a downed drone.

426
00:15:16,325 --> 00:15:17,163
Wait a minute.

427
00:15:17,331 --> 00:15:20,810
Say there was some sort of
top-secret object

428
00:15:20,938 --> 00:15:23,055
hidden somewhere
in Roosevelt High School.

429
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:24,902
Would you two
be able to recover it?

430
00:15:25,033 --> 00:15:27,115
Sue, the Marines aren't helping
you find your chicken head.

431
00:15:27,237 --> 00:15:28,279
It's their day off.

432
00:15:28,629 --> 00:15:31,074
So, Afghanistan-- that must
have been so dangerous.

433
00:15:31,267 --> 00:15:32,980
Well, when you're dealing
with terrorists,

434
00:15:33,124 --> 00:15:34,424
it can get a little sticky.

435
00:15:34,637 --> 00:15:36,892
Well, the real enemy
isn't terrorists.

436
00:15:37,050 --> 00:15:38,558
It's refined sugar.

437
00:15:38,727 --> 00:15:41,328
Kills a hell of a lot more
people than Al Qaeda ever did.

438
00:15:41,456 --> 00:15:42,343
You don't have to talk

439
00:15:42,449 --> 00:15:44,107
everybody's head off
all the time.

440
00:15:44,325 --> 00:15:46,648
You know, they hide from him
at the bank.

441
00:15:46,762 --> 00:15:49,110
You're just jealous 'cause
the weight's falling off of me.

442
00:15:49,283 --> 00:15:51,894
Somebody here has
a love affair with gluten.

443
00:15:52,021 --> 00:15:53,675
Speaking of gluten,
you guys like football?

444
00:15:53,847 --> 00:15:55,887
'Cause, uh, my son here
has got a big game tomorrow.

445
00:15:56,037 --> 00:15:57,859
I don't even
wanna talk about the game.

446
00:15:57,976 --> 00:15:59,499
Why do we have to
talk about the game?

447
00:15:59,678 --> 00:16:01,714
I think I have a pretty good
idea of where it is.

448
00:16:01,855 --> 00:16:04,357
If we go in at nightfall,
I think that would be best.

449
00:16:04,498 --> 00:16:05,479
But I don't have to go

450
00:16:05,593 --> 00:16:06,728
if you think I'm just
gonna get in the way.

451
00:16:06,878 --> 00:16:08,333
I could be sitting
in a nearby van,

452
00:16:08,475 --> 00:16:10,546
talking you through it
over headphones.

453
00:16:10,670 --> 00:16:13,489
(Tag) It was a moonless night.
I was stationed in Korea.

454
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:16,632
- And my boot came untied--
- Everyone's heard the story, Tag.

455
00:16:16,761 --> 00:16:18,499
You tell it every Thanksgiving.

456
00:16:18,626 --> 00:16:19,994
The Marines haven't heard it.

457
00:16:20,116 --> 00:16:23,167
Yes, they have. You've told
that story so many times,

458
00:16:23,291 --> 00:16:24,795
it's gone all the way
around the world,

459
00:16:24,929 --> 00:16:26,811
and even <i>they</i> have heard it.

460
00:16:26,926 --> 00:16:28,051
You know, if you
got some sleep,

461
00:16:28,177 --> 00:16:30,566
- you wouldn't be so cranky.
- And whose fault is that?

462
00:16:30,687 --> 00:16:32,070
You took my side of the bed.

463
00:16:32,189 --> 00:16:34,338
I told you many times,
it's different here.

464
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:35,904
The bed's turned around.

465
00:16:36,025 --> 00:16:38,312
I think I know how to sleep.

466
00:16:38,438 --> 00:16:40,249
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!
(Silverware clatters)

467
00:16:40,409 --> 00:16:42,900
You had your first date
on St. Patrick's Day,

468
00:16:43,035 --> 00:16:44,360
and dad wanted
to take you to the movies,

469
00:16:44,484 --> 00:16:46,312
but he got lost, and you thought
it was so funny.

470
00:16:46,451 --> 00:16:48,340
And you ended up
down by Lake Monroe,

471
00:16:48,478 --> 00:16:49,154
and you were hungry,

472
00:16:49,285 --> 00:16:50,742
so mom shared her saltines
from her purse.

473
00:16:50,913 --> 00:16:51,999
And you were both worried

474
00:16:52,128 --> 00:16:53,471
because the crackers
made your mouth dry

475
00:16:53,609 --> 00:16:55,316
and you thought your first kiss
was gonna be disastrous.

476
00:16:55,451 --> 00:16:57,310
But it wasn't,
because you kissed,

477
00:16:57,453 --> 00:16:58,653
and you felt the earth move,

478
00:16:58,793 --> 00:17:00,185
and you knew you were supposed
to be together

479
00:17:00,323 --> 00:17:02,617
because you loved each other,
damn it!

480
00:17:03,561 --> 00:17:05,124
(Breathing heavily)

481
00:17:05,690 --> 00:17:06,581
(Door opens)

482
00:17:06,991 --> 00:17:07,875
<i>They've been through war,</i>

483
00:17:07,984 --> 00:17:10,059
<i>and they couldn't even</i>
<i>make it to pie.</i>

484
00:17:17,718 --> 00:17:18,670
<i>So as we learned,</i>

485
00:17:18,791 --> 00:17:21,288
<i>Thanksgiving is not</i>
<i>a holiday for observers.</i>

486
00:17:21,543 --> 00:17:22,263
<i>And the next day,</i>

487
00:17:22,387 --> 00:17:25,085
<i>we were still stewing</i>
<i>in our own family juices.</i>

488
00:17:25,272 --> 00:17:26,753
(Players grunting,
crowd cheering)

489
00:17:26,918 --> 00:17:28,000
<i>(Man over PA)</i>
<i>Heck is the ball carrier.</i>

490
00:17:28,655 --> 00:17:29,455
(Thud)

491
00:17:30,122 --> 00:17:31,650
(Whistle blows, crowd groans)

492
00:17:31,761 --> 00:17:32,820
<i>And it's a fumble.</i>

493
00:17:33,641 --> 00:17:35,694
<i>That's Heck's third fumble</i>
<i>of the game.</i>

494
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,448
(Crowd speaking indistinctly)

495
00:17:41,452 --> 00:17:42,798
<i>Sue blamed herself.</i>

496
00:17:42,924 --> 00:17:46,010
<i>Without her mascot head, she</i>
<i>just couldn't bring the spirit.</i>

497
00:17:46,141 --> 00:17:47,849
<i>Luckily, Brad scrounged up</i>
<i>what he could</i>

498
00:17:47,968 --> 00:17:50,319
<i>from his theater camp,</i>
<i>but the thundering chicken bear</i>

499
00:17:50,445 --> 00:17:53,101
<i>didn't exactly</i>
<i>scream confidence.</i>

500
00:17:53,226 --> 00:17:56,062
<i>Wilson drops back to pass.</i>
<i>He finds Axl Heck.</i>

501
00:17:56,196 --> 00:17:57,797
<i>Heck drops the ball!</i>

502
00:17:59,346 --> 00:18:01,713
And I thought
the end of Love Story was sad.

503
00:18:02,416 --> 00:18:03,058
(Crowd groaning)

504
00:18:03,159 --> 00:18:04,227
Time-out. Time-out.

505
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,055
(Whistle blows)

506
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,482
<i>Time-out-- Orson.</i>

507
00:18:06,607 --> 00:18:08,561
Come on, guys!
Bring it in. Bring it in.

508
00:18:12,625 --> 00:18:14,343
Axl, what is going on with you?

509
00:18:14,485 --> 00:18:16,872
I don't know.
I don't know what I'm doing.

510
00:18:16,989 --> 00:18:17,621
I'm trying to focus,

511
00:18:17,745 --> 00:18:19,159
but all these thoughts
keep popping into my head.

512
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:20,643
I keep thinking maybe
I shouldn't have played.

513
00:18:20,796 --> 00:18:22,073
And then I think
I should be studying more.

514
00:18:22,195 --> 00:18:23,639
Then I think what if I hurt
my foot even worse?

515
00:18:23,736 --> 00:18:24,830
I'm freaking myself out here!

516
00:18:24,962 --> 00:18:27,253
Axl, that's your problem.
You're thinking too much.

517
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:28,402
What?

518
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,495
Everything good that's ever
happened to you in your life

519
00:18:30,631 --> 00:18:32,900
happened because
you weren't thinking.

520
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:36,545
Look at me. Look at me!
(Grunts)

521
00:18:38,282 --> 00:18:39,472
The only way
you're gonna win this game

522
00:18:39,606 --> 00:18:42,371
is if you go out there
and do what you do best.

523
00:18:42,486 --> 00:18:45,140
Don't think.
You get back out there,

524
00:18:45,275 --> 00:18:47,956
turn your brain off,
and win this game!

525
00:18:48,762 --> 00:18:50,250
<i>Sometimes the wisest advice</i>

526
00:18:50,382 --> 00:18:52,615
<i>comes from the mouths</i>
<i>of chicken bears.</i>

527
00:18:52,738 --> 00:18:55,026
- Go!
- Yes! Whoo!

528
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:56,676
(Thud)

529
00:19:02,159 --> 00:19:03,196
<i>The hand-off goes to Heck.</i>

530
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:05,525
<i>He runs left.</i>
<i>Heck reverses field!</i>

531
00:19:05,688 --> 00:19:08,196
<i>Heck is running</i>
<i>for the wrong end zone!</i>

532
00:19:08,336 --> 00:19:09,379
What is he thinking?!

533
00:19:09,970 --> 00:19:11,387
(Squeals) He's not!

534
00:19:12,952 --> 00:19:15,005
(Cheering)

535
00:19:15,618 --> 00:19:17,731
Go, go, go, go!
Go! Yes!

536
00:19:18,364 --> 00:19:20,093
(Cheering)

537
00:19:23,394 --> 00:19:24,856
Touchdown. Yeah!

538
00:19:27,164 --> 00:19:28,438
Whoo!

539
00:19:33,201 --> 00:19:36,219
<i>Sue's speech worked.</i>
<i>Once Axl stopped thinking,</i>

540
00:19:36,441 --> 00:19:37,780
<i>he scored two more touchdowns</i>

541
00:19:37,888 --> 00:19:40,215
<i>and led his team</i>
<i>to the city championship.</i>

542
00:19:40,901 --> 00:19:42,286
(Whistle blows)

543
00:19:42,938 --> 00:19:45,243
(Cheering continues)

544
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:55,443
Hey! That was one hell
of a second half

545
00:19:55,576 --> 00:19:57,011
you played there, Heck.

546
00:19:57,264 --> 00:19:59,766
I'm really hoping to see you
and that healed foot of yours

547
00:19:59,889 --> 00:20:01,399
at East Indy next year.

548
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:03,633
Yeah? Me and my foot
would love that.

549
00:20:03,764 --> 00:20:05,629
All right! Go, Dragons!

550
00:20:05,813 --> 00:20:07,469
(Laughs) (Laughs)
(Exhales deeply)

551
00:20:12,210 --> 00:20:13,992
(Whooping and laughing)

552
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,102
Hey.

553
00:20:23,489 --> 00:20:24,579
(Sighs) Hey.

554
00:20:25,642 --> 00:20:27,478
<i>That</i> was an amazing game.

555
00:20:27,603 --> 00:20:29,168
I've never seen
anything like it.

556
00:20:29,827 --> 00:20:31,104
I'm not gonna tell you
you were awesome,

557
00:20:31,221 --> 00:20:33,024
'cause you already <i>think</i>
you're awesome.

558
00:20:33,155 --> 00:20:34,588
But that was pretty awesome.

559
00:20:34,741 --> 00:20:36,482
Wait, you--
you saw the game?

560
00:20:36,579 --> 00:20:37,814
I thought you had dinner
with your boyfriend.

561
00:20:37,936 --> 00:20:40,299
Yeah, well,
that kind of got cut short

562
00:20:40,408 --> 00:20:42,949
when I told him
that I like somebody else.

563
00:20:43,475 --> 00:20:44,570
You like somebody else?

564
00:20:44,834 --> 00:20:47,239
Yeah. You.

565
00:20:47,422 --> 00:20:48,758
Oh. (Laughs)

566
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:51,416
Sorry, I've been told
not to think. (Chuckles)

567
00:20:52,227 --> 00:20:53,524
Do you have any plans?

568
00:20:53,646 --> 00:20:56,721
Yeah, but...
I can blow 'em off.

569
00:20:56,883 --> 00:20:58,287
What'd you have in mind?

570
00:20:59,142 --> 00:21:00,244
This.

571
00:21:04,983 --> 00:21:07,423
<i>We never did quite get why</i>
<i>Brick loved that book so much.</i>

572
00:21:07,591 --> 00:21:10,404
<i>Maybe it's 'cause everyone</i>
<i>loves a great love story.</i>

573
00:21:10,547 --> 00:21:12,644
<i>Whether it's that magical</i>
<i>moment at the beginning</i>

574
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:14,542
<i>when everything</i>
<i>is new and exciting,</i>

575
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:17,412
<i>or even when</i>
<i>it's not so new and exciting.</i>

576
00:21:17,644 --> 00:21:19,921
(Pat) What are you doing?
We're supposed to be on I-70.

577
00:21:20,081 --> 00:21:22,028
(Tag) I'm not taking 70.
I know a shortcut.

578
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:24,106
Oh, God, not another shortcut.

579
00:21:24,412 --> 00:21:26,314
We'll be lucky
if we're home by Christmas.

580
00:21:26,430 --> 00:21:28,180
Fine, fine. We'll take 70.

581
00:21:28,637 --> 00:21:30,816
But only because you're cute.
(Chuckles)

582
00:21:30,951 --> 00:21:33,262
Oh. (Laughs)

583
00:21:33,952 --> 00:21:35,782
<i>After all,</i>
<i>the greatest love stories</i>

584
00:21:35,904 --> 00:21:37,877
<i>are the ones that last forever.</i>

585
00:21:38,825 --> 00:21:42,821
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

